H7163.strongs:
Origin: from 7161 and 6320; horn of cosmetic;
Meaning: Keren-hap-Puk, one of Job's daughters
KJV renders: Keren-happuch.

H7165.strongs:
Origin: from 7164;
Meaning: a knob or belaying-pin (from its swelling form)
KJV renders: tache.

H7166.strongs:
Origin: from 7164;
Meaning: an ankle (as a protuberance or joint)
KJV renders: foot.

H7167.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to rend, literally or figuratively (revile, paint the eyes, as if enlarging them)
KJV renders: cut out, rend, × surely, tear.

H7168.strongs:
Origin: from 7167;
Meaning: a rag
KJV renders: piece, rag.

H7169.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to pinch, i.e. (partially) to bite the lips, blink the eyes (as a gesture of malice), or (fully) to squeeze off (a piece of clay in order to mould a vessel from it)
KJV renders: form, move, wink.

H7171.strongs:
Origin: from 7169;
Meaning: extirpation (as if by constriction)
KJV renders: destruction.

H7172.strongs:
Origin: from 7167;
Meaning: floor (as if a pavement of pieces or tesseræ), of a building or the sea
KJV renders: bottom, (× one side of the) floor.

H7173.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7172; ground-floor;
Meaning: Karka (with the article prefix), a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Karkaa.

H7174.strongs:
Origin: from 6979; foundation;
Meaning: Karkor, a place East of the Jordan
KJV renders: Karkor.

H7175.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to split off;
Meaning: a slab or plank; by implication, a deck of a ship
KJV renders: bench, board.

H7176.strongs:
Origin: from 7136 in the sense of building;
Meaning: a city
KJV renders: city.

H7177.strongs:
Origin: from 7176; city;
Meaning: Kartah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Kartah.

H7178.strongs:
Origin: from 7176; city-plot;
Meaning: Kartan, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Kartan.

H7179.strongs:
Origin: from 7197;
Meaning: straw (as dry)
KJV renders: stubble.

H7180.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (meaning to be hard);
Meaning: a cucumber (from the difficulty of digestion)
KJV renders: cucumber.

H7181.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to prick up the ears, i.e. hearken
KJV renders: attend, (cause to) hear(-ken), give heed, incline, mark (well), regard.

H7182.strongs:
Origin: from 7181;
Meaning: a hearkening
KJV renders: × diligently, hearing, much heed, that regarded.

H7183.strongs:
Origin: or קַשֻּׁב; from 7181;
Meaning: hearkening
KJV renders: attent(-ive).

H7184.strongs:
Origin: or קַשְׂוָה; from an unused root meaning to be round;
Meaning: a jug (from its shape)
KJV renders: cover, cup.

H7185.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to be dense, i.e. tough or severe (in various applications)
KJV renders: be cruel, be fiercer, make grievous, be ((ask a), be in, have, seem, would) hard(-en, (labour), -ly, thing), be sore, (be, make) stiff(-en, (-necked)).

H7186.strongs:
Origin: from 7185;
Meaning: severe (in various applications)
KJV renders: churlish, cruel, grievous, hard((-hearted), thing), heavy, impudent, obstinate, prevailed, rough(-ly), sore, sorrowful, stiff(necked), stubborn, in trouble.

H7187.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) or קשֹׁט; (Aramaic), corresponding to 7189;
Meaning: fidelity
KJV renders: truth.

H7188.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to be (causatively, make) unfeeling
KJV renders: harden.

H7189.strongs:
Origin: or קֹשְׁטְ; from an unused root meaning to balance;
Meaning: equity (as evenly weighed), i.e. reality
KJV renders: truth.

H7190.strongs:
Origin: from 7185;
Meaning: obstinacy
KJV renders: stubbornness.

H7191.strongs:
Origin: from 7190; hard ground;
Meaning: Kishjon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Kishion, Keshon.

H7192.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root (probably meaning to weigh out);
Meaning: an ingot (as definitely estimated and stamped for a coin)
KJV renders: piece of money (silver).

H7193.strongs:
Origin: by reduplication from an unused root meaning to shale off as bark;
Meaning: a scale (of a fish); hence a coat of mail (as composed of or covered with jointed plates of metal)
KJV renders: mail, scale.

H7194.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tie, physically (gird, confine, compact) or mentally (in love, league)
KJV renders: bind (up), (make a) conspire(-acy, -ator), join together, knit, stronger, work (treason).

H7195.strongs:
Origin: from 7194;
Meaning: an (unlawful) alliance
KJV renders: confederacy, conspiracy, treason.

H7196.strongs:
Origin: from 7194;
Meaning: an (ornamental) girdle (for women)
KJV renders: attire, headband.

H7197.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root; to become sapless through drought; used only as denominative from 7179;
Meaning: to forage for straw, stubble or wood; figuratively, to assemble
KJV renders: gather (selves) (together).

H7198.strongs:
Origin: from 7185 in the original sense (of 6983) of bending;
Meaning: a bow, for shooting (hence, figuratively, strength) or the iris
KJV renders: × arch(-er), arrow, bow(-man, -shot).

H7199.strongs:
Origin: intensive (as denominative) from 7198;
Meaning: a bowman
KJV renders: × archer.
